{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And there was a king in Jeshurun.</b> Every one of the sons of Levi would say that there was a king in Israel, and He is the Holy One, blessed be He. The meaning is that the Shekhinah dwelt in Israel, and therefore he mentioned Jeshurun, which is a term of seeing, because they saw at Sinai the glory of the Shekhinah eye to eye, and there the heads of the people assembled together — the tribes of Israel — to accept His divinity and His kingship." "<b>By way of the Midrash:</b> ״ויהי בישרון מלך״ — this is Moses, for all Israel heard the Torah expounded from his mouth, and the meaning is that he was like a king, and the heads of the tribes assembled to him; and so it is written above (Deuteronomy 31): ״ואתם אל הכהנים בני לוי״, and it is written (ibid.): ״הקהילו אלי את כל ראשי שבטיכם״. ״ויהי בישרון מלך״ — this is the Holy One, blessed be He. When? When the heads of the people assembled. And so it says (Psalms 47): ״נדיבי עמים נאספו עם אלהי אברהם״ — at the time they assembled. And thus Scripture says (Amos 9): ״הבונה בשמים מעלותיו ואגדתו על ארץ יסדה״, etc. When does He build in the heavens His steps? At the time ״אגדתו על ארץ יסדה״." "<b>By way of the Kabbalah:</b> ״ויהי בישרון מלך״ — this is the attribute of Malkhut, which is comprised of all the rungs. And from this they expounded in Midrash Rabbah on (Amos 9): ״הבונה בשמים מעלותיו ואגודתו על ארץ יסדה״ — to what is the matter likened? To a palace built upon ships: as long as the ships are joined together, the palace upon them stands. Thus ״הבונה בשמים מעלותיו״ — when? When Israel are one ״אגודה״. But when they are not one ״אגודה״, as it were, His throne is destabilized above. It is written מעלתו (his rung) and read מעלותיו (his rungs): the reading alludes to the ten rungs, and what is written alludes to the final rung that comprises them all. If so, Scripture suspended the entire upper structure upon Israel when they are one ״אגודה״." "<b>And know</b> that the word ״ויהי״ teaches that this king is the blessed El. And furthermore, in the word ״ויהי״ there are three combinations in the special Name, when you combine the special Name into four combinations like the ״פרי החג״ (fruit of the festival — i.e., the four species), and the yod alone will be in the fourth combination. And since the word ״ויהי״ is derived from the special Name, this indicates that לה׳ המלוכה. If so, the term מלך in this verse is like the expression (Psalms 145): ״ארוממך אלהי המלך״, which is a teru'ah of a king; and like the expression (Ecclesiastes 5): ״מלך לשדה נעבד״; and like the expression (Song of Songs 7): ״מלך אסור ברהטים״; and likewise (Psalms 24): ״ה' צבאות הוא מלך הכבוד סלה״ — a king who is the kavod (glory). And he said סלה because He is exalted on high unto ein sof (infinity); and the מלך הכבוד he mentioned first is the one who rules over the kavod, and this is clear."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {1 "Citation דברים ל״א: the first quotation (ואתם אל הכהנים בני לוי) does not correspond to Deuteronomy 31:9 (ותכתב משה את התורה); the Hebrew text appears to abbreviate or conflate; the second quotation matches Deuteronomy 31:28."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:54:01.434224122Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}